#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096447 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48a66a99-6b4a-5ad5-8922-6f48006ff183" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "2a61b115-4e26-5966-b2a9-d2fedef6b728" :question/math-academy-id "e-4282" :question/problem "The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ has magnitude $3$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$." :question/worked-solution "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$, we divide $\\mathbf{a}$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=\\dfrac{\\mathbf{a}}{\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a}\\, \\mid}=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\mathbf{a}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096448 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d44ac67b-5e3d-5b1e-bf2c-554b592ba29e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Vector Sum"}] :question/id #uuid "23d9a601-974b-51c2-a6ea-0ebadde19efc" :question/math-academy-id "e-4283" :question/problem "The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $10$, while the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ is directed vertically down and has magnitude $20$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a+b}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $\\mathbf{a+b}$. According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$ goes from the tail of $\\mathbf{a}$ to the head of $\\mathbf{b}$:\n\n![](images/32/32c48d8c19fc68fbc172b240ded922f3e2ebc12804411c318ff63fe999aaedcc.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $\\mathbf{a+b}$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + b}{\\mid a + b \\mid}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}a + b & ^{2} &= & a & ^{2} +\\left.\\end{vmatrix}b\\right|^{2} \\\\\n&= 10^{2} + 20^{2} \\\\\n&= 100 + 400 \\\\\n&= 500\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid \\mathbf{a+b} &= \\sqrt{500}=10\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + b}{\\mid a + b \\mid} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10\\sqrt{5}}(a + b)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096493 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b11642dd-80cc-539c-8c2d-8cdee58e9d3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector in a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "6dfe09f0-30e2-53bc-a8f6-d7e4a3b8232a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5181" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d3042242136b82b867b8bd7911761ee38318924df0c9979488d20f04117c45d9.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf a$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/b3/b316448c885a20a7ed60871ce0f1a4dc4f77bd4658dc6eda3407fb3c89a088cb.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have\n\n$$\n\\angle AHB = 90^\\circ\n$$\n\n, $AH=3$ and $BH=2$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^{2} + BH^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{3^{2} + 2^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$ is $\\sqrt{13}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{\\mid a \\mid} \\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48a66a99-6b4a-5ad5-8922-6f48006ff183" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fdcd9ee-41aa-59b2-9679-818cb4084f32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571565} {:answer/id #uuid "52dd74f0-57c8-5c05-a6c9-94f401433860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571690} {:answer/id #uuid "732d5801-52f2-5d98-acd2-59cdcfe05a95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571734} {:answer/id #uuid "8c59c84a-5a15-5e0e-a1f6-c99349e42bf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571780} {:answer/id #uuid "afa2cd68-68c4-597f-8279-d2ad3f802291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c59c84a-5a15-5e0e-a1f6-c99349e42bf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571780} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb846a7c-a839-56a8-a16b-0c31f3561ba1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572104}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9630409b-82f5-5e41-add3-624263d041a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-11377" :question/problem "The vector $b$ has magnitude $20.$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $b.$" :question/worked-solution "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $b$, we divide $b$ by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{b}{|\\,b\\,|}=\\frac{1}{20}b\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48a66a99-6b4a-5ad5-8922-6f48006ff183" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "052d695c-75c2-537a-b2dd-d40fb706a504" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}\\overset{\\to }{UV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571549} {:answer/id #uuid "2b72b380-5234-5f6a-925b-f6a08d294796" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{UV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571611} {:answer/id #uuid "31d03316-8870-51ff-8acc-393b2704b5f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\overset{\\to }{UV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571623} {:answer/id #uuid "4d4e311b-d223-5cb9-82e6-b49ae0b379b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\overset{\\to }{UV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571678} {:answer/id #uuid "77bdcaf2-bbad-5bfa-a013-fc5cd78f7ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\overset{\\to }{UV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77bdcaf2-bbad-5bfa-a013-fc5cd78f7ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\overset{\\to }{UV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571743} :answer-field/id #uuid "537d3cf5-0d6e-5a1b-96fe-52ba35118a33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572020}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec3ac6e6-c786-5106-a626-b9bded90e31e" :question/math-academy-id "q-119788" :question/problem "The vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$ has magnitude $\\frac{1}{3}.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $\\overset{\\to }{UV}?$" :question/worked-solution "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $\\overset{\\to }{UV},$ we divide $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$ by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{UV}}{|\\overset{\\to }{UV}|}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{3})}\\overset{\\to }{UV}=3\\overset{\\to }{UV}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572109 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48a66a99-6b4a-5ad5-8922-6f48006ff183" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a6a3e04-07dd-5e46-ac74-a50abff88f06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571777} {:answer/id #uuid "9a640bc5-fe07-5407-ae3b-8c6cef3acf65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571806} {:answer/id #uuid "b62dfa05-6c38-5ac9-b766-251c1de1c15f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571858} {:answer/id #uuid "dfe39d07-065f-50d1-be1f-6581aaaea180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571940} {:answer/id #uuid "ee1f63f0-d8dc-5fec-a4d6-2f15fec3ad73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b62dfa05-6c38-5ac9-b766-251c1de1c15f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571858} :answer-field/id #uuid "4718ed5c-b264-549b-898b-519d897a84b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ea2b07d-a05f-5f3d-9418-d56ab52d7fcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-119791" :question/problem "The vector $m$ has magnitude $\\frac{7}{2}.$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $m.$" :question/worked-solution "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $m$, we divide $m$ by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{m}{|\\,m\\,|}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{7}{2})}m=\\frac{2}{7}m\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b11642dd-80cc-539c-8c2d-8cdee58e9d3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector in a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "133b9a0b-07a3-5279-9f37-33049aaaa2e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{29}}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571572} {:answer/id #uuid "b626256e-983a-5f2c-9230-3938cb23814d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571857} {:answer/id #uuid "b80ef2f2-4a9b-5e69-872c-2881d1a0e191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{29}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571864} {:answer/id #uuid "c245d639-18f5-577d-a798-c53b48699ba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{29}}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571885} {:answer/id #uuid "f784eacd-53c7-568d-957e-7b132d8f2939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{29}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c245d639-18f5-577d-a798-c53b48699ba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{29}}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571885} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3de6837-e66c-5b9a-a142-8fdce8446005" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb1f02a3-6465-553f-a943-f356abc8fd01" :question/math-academy-id "q-119796" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aa72f6ea8c52a1f141f8469c3f932937b8b957956dc478811910e77c83336a9c.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $p?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/4d/4d4d7faa0c0611c8ef891cda5fef3b75a61aa97e0879fac525f58f4ce263c937.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$, we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=2$ and $BH=5.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $p$ is $\\sqrt{29}.$ Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{|\\,p\\,|}\\cdot p \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{29}}p.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b11642dd-80cc-539c-8c2d-8cdee58e9d3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector in a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae96c78f-e10d-563b-82af-e2c02160928e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{29}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094940} {:answer/id #uuid "25f7a90e-939a-568d-ba3d-07a616fcb021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{q + r}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094941} {:answer/id #uuid "328e6ad2-ef2f-5827-8881-60cdfaebb76b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2q}{\\sqrt{13}} + \\frac{r}{\\sqrt{29}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094942} {:answer/id #uuid "681555fa-cdb3-5281-b943-0cf1eed80c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2(q + r))/(\\sqrt{73})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094943} {:answer/id #uuid "703e463a-8826-5adf-9d3d-36bfd8037d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{q + r}{\\sqrt{13}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094944}] :answer-field/id #uuid "96962338-e491-50f7-b8da-1efc8b69ba83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9d05ca0e-131b-5294-8367-1760396e4369" :question/math-academy-id "q-19276" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9dfaf74a497a2fd22428e09a4c26d573e184c9728ccf67f11ebb9d6a2a44f4c6.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $q + r$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b11642dd-80cc-539c-8c2d-8cdee58e9d3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector in a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6bcf0a9-648c-5969-b70f-729de3275926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}(p+q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6bcf0a9-648c-5969-b70f-729de3275926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}(p+q)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571924} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a9adad1-9941-5e52-a6d0-5821492aa5a4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572053}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bf062e19-facf-5f56-9031-7ed68b8d30bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-275627" :question/problem "![](images/13/13fc8ff564a7162c556d050a10df6e8f23c0fca269e3b88168ca6681be3ad3a3.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Find a unit vector $u$ that is parallel to  $p+q$ and has the same direction as $p+q.$ \n\nType $p$ and $q$ to represent the vectors $p$ and $q,$ respectively.  \n\n$u=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $p+q.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $p+q$ goes from the tail of $p$ to the head of $q:$ \n\n![](images/68/68c14ce5ff66272986e958f09f30289d56519e90b34fae23362753f84c042a50.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$, we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=2$ and $BH=3.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|p+q| & =AB \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $p+q$ is $\\sqrt{13}.$ Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{|p+q|}\\cdot (p+q) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}(p+q).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d44ac67b-5e3d-5b1e-bf2c-554b592ba29e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Vector Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0294dd84-5297-5c6e-8070-0e3be90f9787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0294dd84-5297-5c6e-8070-0e3be90f9787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{a+b}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571540} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0b511d2-5952-5b68-a426-4cf5aaba9091" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572064}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "46e2433f-faec-5a20-b0d6-cabb5029813a" :question/math-academy-id "q-275632" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $\\sqrt{3}$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically up and has magnitude $\\sqrt{6}.$ Find a unit vector $u$ that is parallel to  $a+b$ and has the same direction as $a+b.$ \n\nType $a$ and $b$ to represent the vectors $a$ and $b,$ respectively.  \n\n$u=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$ \n\n![](images/b7/b7d45d7cd1ea2c61961da8279d3f8702d3e52092fc6aab75a94d3b5076928dba.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =3+6 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{9}=3,\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48a66a99-6b4a-5ad5-8922-6f48006ff183" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2057facb-9b8a-526c-a11c-3348083b8b00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\overset{\\to }{ST}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571595} {:answer/id #uuid "7b810dad-7762-5fad-9f57-62184f819cf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{ST}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571751} {:answer/id #uuid "863033f0-b097-59ec-83fe-30cc1e87a732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\overset{\\to }{ST}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571769} {:answer/id #uuid "9adea805-868a-56ca-bb88-e78a3fc0bb38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\overset{\\to }{ST}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571807} {:answer/id #uuid "d19c6a17-6128-503a-91a5-8be8628fed91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\overset{\\to }{ST}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "863033f0-b097-59ec-83fe-30cc1e87a732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\overset{\\to }{ST}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571769} :answer-field/id #uuid "b902b0a7-5e71-5e88-9ec6-9f63e578d722" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50b46995-90d3-558d-b802-06393c983f30" :question/math-academy-id "q-69977" :question/problem "The vector $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ has magnitude $6.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $\\overset{\\to }{ST}?$" :question/worked-solution "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $\\overset{\\to }{ST},$ we divide $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{ST}}{|\\overset{\\to }{ST}|}=\\frac{1}{6}\\overset{\\to }{ST}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d44ac67b-5e3d-5b1e-bf2c-554b592ba29e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Vector Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0da18e66-19b8-54da-a811-7bff65f316a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}(a+b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571563} {:answer/id #uuid "39a84a6a-bccf-512e-adc7-a3b19071646f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}(a+b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571642} {:answer/id #uuid "c168b279-f15c-5669-a575-1c75c357532e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}(a+b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571883} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e39e22-a209-599e-8108-7f028d51f9b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{17}(a+b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571921} {:answer/id #uuid "d726cf39-50e8-5e85-a32e-868dc97d0467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{173}}(a+b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0da18e66-19b8-54da-a811-7bff65f316a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}(a+b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571563} :answer-field/id #uuid "85ffb2ee-f378-58a7-b51e-ef917e3a8dac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2f3e6ef6-a3b7-556b-876b-54d269e801f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-77227" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed due north-west and $|\\,a\\,|=5$, while the vector $b$ is directed due south-west and $|\\,b\\,|=12.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$   \n\n![](images/15/153aff405a3ae0859ff74fcb98deb09e038db7b033cbe54223866c9fe1724fb1.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={5}^{2}+{12}^{2} \\\\  & =169\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{169}=13,\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572138 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d44ac67b-5e3d-5b1e-bf2c-554b592ba29e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Vector Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25d977df-2058-5b96-8d7e-8459946ef00d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}(a+b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571602} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4ca2cc-f364-53e7-b5d7-754b69c071d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{98}(a+b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571672} {:answer/id #uuid "926b8523-c3d4-5e8e-b28f-59156da36f88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7\\sqrt{2}}(a+b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571798} {:answer/id #uuid "c628653b-f32f-521c-a5ac-5e6e7ac0095c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{6}}(a+b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571891} {:answer/id #uuid "c76d32fd-0d07-5a6f-a42b-f98aee2a62ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}(a+b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "926b8523-c3d4-5e8e-b28f-59156da36f88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7\\sqrt{2}}(a+b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571798} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecbe05ce-5c99-5a55-b52c-2b92b42e1761" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572093}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "64f8dbbc-bd8d-5e6e-b9e2-32a2e83cd44b" :question/math-academy-id "q-77229" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed due north-east and $|\\,a\\,|=7$, while the vector $b$ is directed due north-west and $|\\,b\\,|=7.$ Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $a+b$ goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $b:$   \n\n![](images/94/9468530a650f0bee117a4254aa87b5954c7bbbe2684d95f9db3f9961026abcb2.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b,$ we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{|a+b|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={7}^{2}+{7}^{2} \\\\  & =98\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{98}=7\\sqrt{2},\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7\\sqrt{2}}(a+b).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
